1
00:00:06,050 --> 00:00:11,330
<i>Our story began one fateful day...</i>

2
00:00:27,100 --> 00:00:29,760
<i>I wasn't pretending to sleep</i>

3
00:00:29,760 --> 00:00:33,300
<i>in the warm, spring sun.</i>

4
00:00:33,300 --> 00:00:38,860
<i>This is just how I spend my breaks in peace,</i>

5
00:00:38,860 --> 00:00:43,900
<i>as a guy with no friends in his class.</i>

6
00:00:49,100 --> 00:00:51,810
That's all for our stream today.

7
00:00:51,810 --> 00:00:53,130
Sorry guys.

8
00:00:53,130 --> 00:00:55,170
- See you in the next one.
- Bye for now.

9
00:00:55,170 --> 00:00:57,130
- And done.
- Cool.

10
00:00:57,130 --> 00:00:58,910
- How about a post-stream selfie?
- Sure.

11
00:00:58,910 --> 00:01:00,240
Wanna join in, Asamiya?

12
00:01:00,240 --> 00:01:01,270
No thanks.

13
00:01:01,270 --> 00:01:03,240
- Sure. You ready?
- Always.

14
00:01:17,360 --> 00:01:19,760
Dude, I'm not in the shot.

15
00:01:19,760 --> 00:01:21,690
Fix your aim.

16
00:01:41,460 --> 00:01:46,960
It's been one month since the semester began.

17
00:01:46,960 --> 00:01:49,700
Which means it's time to change seats.

18
00:01:49,700 --> 00:01:52,050
- Seriously?
- Score!

19
00:01:52,050 --> 00:01:55,450
Seats will be chosen at random.

20
00:01:58,070 --> 00:01:59,930
Come draw your lot.

21
00:01:59,930 --> 00:02:01,340
And don't dawdle.

22
00:02:06,810 --> 00:02:08,330
Next.

23
00:02:17,950 --> 00:02:19,810
Next.

24
00:02:19,810 --> 00:02:22,790
- I'm over there!
- Screw you, man.

25
00:02:26,080 --> 00:02:27,230
I got a great spot.

26
00:02:27,230 --> 00:02:28,640
Man, I hate being up front.

27
00:02:28,640 --> 00:02:29,890
Yeah, I'll be right in the teacher's vision.

28
00:02:29,890 --> 00:02:31,530
Let's swap.

29
00:02:31,530 --> 00:02:34,660
- You need the front seat.
- My eyesight's not that bad.

30
00:02:40,770 --> 00:02:44,180
<i>This is fine.</i>

31
00:02:48,470 --> 00:02:53,190
<i>I like my ordinary, uneventful life.</i>

32
00:03:08,550 --> 00:03:11,020
Everyone situated?

33
00:03:11,020 --> 00:03:14,770
Then pass your worksheets up front.

34
00:03:15,450 --> 00:03:18,220
Settle down already.

35
00:03:24,800 --> 00:03:26,250
<i>Huh?</i>

36
00:03:35,480 --> 00:03:39,940
<i>I thought I was just fine with the ordinary.</i>

37
00:03:41,760 --> 00:03:47,660
<i>But this one seat change</i>

38
00:03:49,250 --> 00:03:53,590
<i>flipped my mundane high school life</i>

39
00:03:53,590 --> 00:03:55,980
<i>right upside down.</i>

40
00:03:55,980 --> 00:04:02,150
[I like you.]

41
00:04:40,330 --> 00:04:44,350
[Adapted from Mashiroito's work of the same title]

42
00:04:50,670 --> 00:04:52,180
I'll take this one.

43
00:04:55,690 --> 00:04:57,990
<i>Today's the day I get one.</i>

44
00:04:57,990 --> 00:05:00,160
<i>Because if I don't...</i>

45
00:05:00,160 --> 00:05:01,170
Easy now.

46
00:05:01,170 --> 00:05:03,240
[Principal's Original Bread! Just 120 Yen]

47
00:05:03,240 --> 00:05:05,140
Here you are.

48
00:05:05,140 --> 00:05:06,320
Thanks, ma'am.

49
00:05:06,320 --> 00:05:08,370
I'll take this one.

50
00:05:08,370 --> 00:05:09,550
That'll be 180 yen.

51
00:05:09,550 --> 00:05:10,960
Of course.

52
00:05:10,960 --> 00:05:12,830
Excuse me.

53
00:05:12,830 --> 00:05:14,950
Are you sold out today?

54
00:05:14,950 --> 00:05:18,150
- Yes, so sorry.
- Aw man...

55
00:05:18,150 --> 00:05:20,580
He's gonna blow his fuse again...

56
00:05:25,740 --> 00:05:27,610
Here.

57
00:05:27,610 --> 00:05:29,290
Have this last one.

58
00:05:29,290 --> 00:05:31,440
- You sure?
- Yeah.

59
00:05:31,440 --> 00:05:32,780
Thanks!

60
00:05:32,780 --> 00:05:34,710
- I'll take this.
- That'll be 180 yen.

61
00:05:34,710 --> 00:05:36,360
Mayama.

62
00:05:36,360 --> 00:05:38,070
I've still got plenty right here.

63
00:05:40,210 --> 00:05:43,080
Then I'll take one.

64
00:05:43,080 --> 00:05:44,990
That'll be 120 yen.

65
00:05:44,990 --> 00:05:46,640
Right.

66
00:05:48,110 --> 00:05:49,230
Here you are.

67
00:05:49,230 --> 00:05:51,420
Thanks for purchasing.

68
00:05:51,420 --> 00:05:54,040
I'll always have some in stock.

69
00:06:15,310 --> 00:06:20,700
<i>What was with that note this morning?</i>

70
00:06:20,700 --> 00:06:23,080
[I like you.]

71
00:06:24,480 --> 00:06:28,750
<i>Is he pranking me?</i>

72
00:06:28,750 --> 00:06:32,050
<i>No one would fall for this.</i>

73
00:06:32,050 --> 00:06:34,690
<i>We're an all-boys school.</i>

74
00:06:35,590 --> 00:06:37,840
Could I get your worksheets?

75
00:06:41,910 --> 00:06:45,270
Asamiya, um...

76
00:06:45,270 --> 00:06:46,820
Your note here.

77
00:06:55,660 --> 00:06:59,440
Window row, you almost done?

78
00:07:06,130 --> 00:07:09,510
If you're going to erase it,
why write anything at all?

79
00:07:13,570 --> 00:07:15,320
<i>Hold on.</i>

80
00:07:16,000 --> 00:07:20,680
<i>What if that note wasn't a prank?</i>

81
00:07:22,860 --> 00:07:26,050
No way...

82
00:07:26,050 --> 00:07:30,610
<i>Was Asamiya confessing to someone in our row?</i>

83
00:07:33,260 --> 00:07:35,270
No, impossible.

84
00:07:35,270 --> 00:07:37,850
I'm jumping to wild conclusions.

85
00:07:47,510 --> 00:07:50,410
Ms. Komori?

86
00:07:54,890 --> 00:07:58,900
<i>No, that can't be it.</i>

87
00:07:58,900 --> 00:08:00,960
<i>Right?</i>

88
00:08:00,960 --> 00:08:03,430
<i>I don't know.</i>

89
00:08:03,430 --> 00:08:05,450
<i>Maybe he likes older women.</i>

90
00:08:05,450 --> 00:08:10,130
<i>Wait, does that mean I got in his way?</i>

91
00:08:11,650 --> 00:08:13,590
This is bad.

92
00:08:13,590 --> 00:08:15,250
This is bad.

93
00:08:15,250 --> 00:08:18,920
This is really, really bad.

94
00:08:18,920 --> 00:08:21,640
<i>Because Asamiya, he's...</i>

95
00:08:22,660 --> 00:08:25,190
<i>He's got the brains and the looks.</i>

96
00:08:25,190 --> 00:08:28,450
<i>He's the highest tier guy in our school.</i>

97
00:08:29,280 --> 00:08:34,350
<i>If I actually did piss him off,
my high school career is over.</i>

98
00:08:36,210 --> 00:08:38,280
His smile, it's too bright...

99
00:08:38,280 --> 00:08:39,580
What are you doing?

100
00:08:39,580 --> 00:08:41,490
Huh?

101
00:08:41,490 --> 00:08:43,130
It's the real deal.

102
00:08:43,130 --> 00:08:44,630
Huh?

103
00:08:46,180 --> 00:08:47,700
Nothing.

104
00:08:48,320 --> 00:08:52,300
<i>What? What now?</i>

105
00:08:55,010 --> 00:08:57,240
Mind if I join you?

106
00:08:58,530 --> 00:08:59,980
Huh?

107
00:09:04,500 --> 00:09:07,740
<i>What exactly is going on here?</i>

108
00:09:08,920 --> 00:09:10,580
What's that?

109
00:09:12,420 --> 00:09:14,100
Bread.

110
00:09:14,100 --> 00:09:16,240
Made by the principal.

111
00:09:16,240 --> 00:09:19,810
People actually eat his stuff?

112
00:09:19,810 --> 00:09:23,210
The good bread was sold out.

113
00:09:29,280 --> 00:09:32,920
<i>He's mad... right?</i>

114
00:09:33,560 --> 00:09:35,330
<i>I mean, I think he is.</i>

115
00:09:41,640 --> 00:09:43,350
Asamiya.

116
00:09:45,500 --> 00:09:47,330
That note...

117
00:09:49,750 --> 00:09:52,130
Sorry, I know you weren't expecting it.

118
00:09:52,130 --> 00:09:54,850
You could say that.

119
00:09:57,150 --> 00:09:59,330
But I meant every word.

120
00:09:59,330 --> 00:10:01,040
Sorry.

121
00:10:08,380 --> 00:10:10,120
It's fine.

122
00:10:11,710 --> 00:10:13,380
Don't worry about it.

123
00:10:14,290 --> 00:10:16,740
I didn't realize you were serious.

124
00:10:17,620 --> 00:10:20,110
And here I am, getting in your way...

125
00:10:21,360 --> 00:10:23,020
Huh?

126
00:10:23,020 --> 00:10:26,600
I made you erase your note for Ms. Komori.

127
00:10:26,600 --> 00:10:29,110
- What?
- I'm sorry.

128
00:10:29,110 --> 00:10:32,030
I know apologizing doesn't help, but...

129
00:10:32,030 --> 00:10:33,840
No, that's not...

130
00:10:33,840 --> 00:10:35,820
I'm so, so sorry.

131
00:10:39,790 --> 00:10:43,270
That note was for you.

132
00:10:44,450 --> 00:10:46,310
Right, thought so.

133
00:10:48,310 --> 00:10:49,880
Wait, what?

134
00:10:49,880 --> 00:10:53,040
It was for you.

135
00:10:54,890 --> 00:10:57,600
For me?

136
00:11:04,570 --> 00:11:06,210
Are you pulling my leg?

137
00:11:06,210 --> 00:11:08,040
- No.
- Oh, okay.

138
00:11:08,040 --> 00:11:11,040
So, the note.

139
00:11:12,660 --> 00:11:14,700
Why me?

140
00:11:17,570 --> 00:11:20,510
Because I like you, why else?

141
00:11:21,120 --> 00:11:23,810
Right.

142
00:11:23,810 --> 00:11:25,710
<i>That doesn't answer anything.</i>

143
00:11:25,710 --> 00:11:29,380
This is the first time we've spoken, though.

144
00:11:29,380 --> 00:11:30,760
It's not.

145
00:11:30,760 --> 00:11:32,210
It's not?

146
00:11:34,180 --> 00:11:35,400
I figured you wouldn't remember.

147
00:11:35,400 --> 00:11:37,930
Well, I mean...

148
00:11:40,890 --> 00:11:43,360
What about me do you even...

149
00:11:43,360 --> 00:11:46,010
Asamiya, what's keeping you?

150
00:11:47,060 --> 00:11:48,880
Sorry, be right there.

151
00:12:00,360 --> 00:12:02,140
Mayama.

152
00:12:03,780 --> 00:12:05,820
If you want to know why I like you...

153
00:12:20,960 --> 00:12:23,160
Well, you'll find out.

154
00:12:37,710 --> 00:12:41,920
[Mayama]

155
00:12:41,920 --> 00:12:44,620
I'm so confused.

156
00:12:45,370 --> 00:12:47,090
Why...

157
00:12:47,090 --> 00:12:49,980
<i>Because I like you, why else?</i>

158
00:12:49,980 --> 00:12:51,910
<i>Mayama.</i>

159
00:12:53,400 --> 00:12:55,390
<i>If you want to know why I like you...</i>

160
00:12:56,240 --> 00:12:58,420
<i>Well, you'll find out.</i>

161
00:13:00,630 --> 00:13:03,990
Why me?

162
00:13:13,400 --> 00:13:15,620
- Morning.
- Hey.

163
00:13:15,620 --> 00:13:18,050
Eat quick, or you'll be late.

164
00:13:24,210 --> 00:13:26,860
Mom and Dad already left for work.

165
00:13:27,780 --> 00:13:29,040
You have more trophies.

166
00:13:29,040 --> 00:13:30,610
Huh? Oh.

167
00:13:32,180 --> 00:13:34,780
Anyway, I have to get to work.

168
00:13:37,730 --> 00:13:41,910
I'd understand if he were into my brother…

169
00:13:41,910 --> 00:13:43,890
What was that?

170
00:13:43,890 --> 00:13:45,300
Nothing.

171
00:13:45,300 --> 00:13:47,570
See you later.

172
00:14:04,010 --> 00:14:05,600
Morning.

173
00:14:06,440 --> 00:14:09,270
Morning?

174
00:14:09,270 --> 00:14:11,190
Why are you here?

175
00:14:11,190 --> 00:14:13,270
I was waiting for you.

176
00:14:15,310 --> 00:14:17,120
Hurry, we'll be late.

177
00:14:20,550 --> 00:14:21,930
Huh?

178
00:14:23,010 --> 00:14:24,610
Sorry.

179
00:14:26,600 --> 00:14:28,190
Mayama?

180
00:14:29,370 --> 00:14:31,590
I'm fine.

181
00:14:39,940 --> 00:14:42,130
Everyone got their papers?

182
00:14:42,130 --> 00:14:44,700
<i>What the heck am I doing?</i>

183
00:14:44,700 --> 00:14:47,970
<i>I didn't have to run.</i>

184
00:14:47,970 --> 00:14:50,640
<i>Like me or not,</i>

185
00:14:50,640 --> 00:14:53,580
<i>anyone would be offended by my attitude.</i>

186
00:14:53,580 --> 00:14:55,600
<i>I've got to apologize.</i>

187
00:14:55,600 --> 00:14:59,550
Ready? Begin.

188
00:15:00,510 --> 00:15:02,480
Hey, can I borrow an eraser?

189
00:15:03,300 --> 00:15:04,660
Sure.

190
00:15:31,730 --> 00:15:33,830
Pencils down.

191
00:15:33,830 --> 00:15:36,840
Pass your tests up front.

192
00:15:42,310 --> 00:15:47,520
[Your bed hair, your hunched back]
[You never prioritize yourself]

193
00:15:53,620 --> 00:15:55,790
Right. Of course.

194
00:16:00,120 --> 00:16:01,700
Nothing.

195
00:16:24,690 --> 00:16:27,700
[Your bed hair, your hunched back]
[You never prioritize yourself]

196
00:16:27,700 --> 00:16:28,750
<i>I've got the bread.</i>

197
00:16:28,750 --> 00:16:29,860
<i>There he is!</i>

198
00:16:29,860 --> 00:16:32,910
- <i>Finally!</i>
- <i>Thanks, man.</i>

199
00:16:32,910 --> 00:16:34,560
<i>You're so useful to have around.</i>

200
00:16:34,560 --> 00:16:36,550
<i>Seriously.</i>

201
00:16:36,550 --> 00:16:37,770
<i>I want a croqutte bread.</i>

202
00:16:37,770 --> 00:16:39,620
<i>Could I have one, too?</i>

203
00:16:39,620 --> 00:16:41,080
- <i>Sure.</i>
- <i>Go ahead.</i>

204
00:16:41,080 --> 00:16:42,690
<i>Thanks.</i>

205
00:16:43,680 --> 00:16:46,530
<i>These are all negative traits of mine.</i>

206
00:16:46,530 --> 00:16:51,620
<i>I knew it. Asamiya was just pulling my leg.</i>

207
00:17:01,990 --> 00:17:03,740
Sorry.

208
00:17:05,510 --> 00:17:07,230
Do you have a minute?

209
00:17:20,890 --> 00:17:22,550
Sit.

210
00:17:23,560 --> 00:17:25,050
Sure.

211
00:17:32,170 --> 00:17:34,530
So, what'd you need?

212
00:17:36,600 --> 00:17:39,940
I wanted to clear up the misunderstanding.

213
00:17:39,940 --> 00:17:41,200
Huh?

214
00:17:41,200 --> 00:17:42,860
My sticky notes.

215
00:17:44,790 --> 00:17:48,270
No, you made yourself loud and clear.

216
00:17:49,460 --> 00:17:51,340
If anything, you're helping.

217
00:17:51,340 --> 00:17:54,370
Keep pointing out my bad traits.

218
00:17:56,320 --> 00:18:00,010
I'm sure there's more you've picked up on.

219
00:18:00,930 --> 00:18:04,640
Maybe lots more, actually.

220
00:18:15,070 --> 00:18:17,960
I knew there was a misunderstanding.

221
00:18:17,960 --> 00:18:19,190
Huh?

222
00:18:19,190 --> 00:18:20,890
I wasn't pointing out anything bad.

223
00:18:20,890 --> 00:18:25,280
These are stuff I like about you.

224
00:18:26,670 --> 00:18:28,090
What?

225
00:18:28,090 --> 00:18:30,740
I told you that you'd find out, right?

226
00:18:39,750 --> 00:18:41,290
I like your bedhead.

227
00:18:41,290 --> 00:18:43,930
I like how you hunch over.

228
00:18:45,080 --> 00:18:46,880
And...

229
00:18:49,720 --> 00:18:53,610
<i>You prioritize others,
even at your own expense.</i>

230
00:18:55,290 --> 00:18:57,900
Because you're kind.

231
00:18:59,930 --> 00:19:01,620
Mayama?

232
00:19:03,290 --> 00:19:07,920
No one's ever said that about me before.

233
00:19:09,490 --> 00:19:11,290
Hold on.

234
00:19:14,470 --> 00:19:16,490
Here.

235
00:19:16,490 --> 00:19:19,400
I managed to beat the crowd and get one.

236
00:19:19,400 --> 00:19:21,000
Here, it's all yours.

237
00:19:21,850 --> 00:19:23,680
Thanks.

238
00:19:23,680 --> 00:19:25,650
- How much was it?
- It's fine.

239
00:19:25,650 --> 00:19:27,070
I wanted to buy one.

240
00:19:27,070 --> 00:19:28,310
But I'm the one eating it.

241
00:19:28,310 --> 00:19:30,140
Then how about this.

242
00:19:32,560 --> 00:19:36,960
Can I make a request?

243
00:19:39,360 --> 00:19:41,110
A request?

244
00:19:49,060 --> 00:19:51,330
I want to touch your bed hair.

245
00:19:53,760 --> 00:19:55,720
- What?
- You can say no.

246
00:19:55,720 --> 00:19:59,620
I mean, it's fine.

247
00:20:00,420 --> 00:20:02,730
It just doesn't exactly feel fair?

248
00:20:02,730 --> 00:20:07,410
An opportunity to touch you
is plenty fulfilling for me.

249
00:20:12,050 --> 00:20:14,330
If you insist.

250
00:20:14,330 --> 00:20:15,840
Go ahead.

251
00:20:28,740 --> 00:20:30,180
- Pause.
- What?

252
00:20:30,180 --> 00:20:35,860
If you go slow, it's ticklish.

253
00:20:37,110 --> 00:20:38,970
Relax.

254
00:20:52,560 --> 00:20:54,110
Should I stop?

255
00:20:55,530 --> 00:20:59,030
It's fine.

256
00:21:06,720 --> 00:21:10,190
Sorry I offended you this morning.

257
00:21:12,540 --> 00:21:14,280
This morning?

258
00:21:16,280 --> 00:21:20,560
You waited for me, and I pushed you away.

259
00:21:23,640 --> 00:21:25,310
I wasn't offended.

260
00:21:25,310 --> 00:21:26,840
You weren't?

261
00:21:26,840 --> 00:21:30,850
No. I was too busy admiring you.

262
00:21:33,380 --> 00:21:35,150
I thought I made you hate me.

263
00:21:35,150 --> 00:21:36,980
That'd never happen.

264
00:21:37,890 --> 00:21:42,670
I would never come to hate you.

265
00:21:52,130 --> 00:21:55,570
So, Asamiya.

266
00:21:55,570 --> 00:21:58,310
When you said you "liked" me...

267
00:22:01,710 --> 00:22:03,360
Never mind.

268
00:22:03,360 --> 00:22:05,050
What?

269
00:22:15,780 --> 00:22:17,470
You got some on your cheek.

270
00:22:30,130 --> 00:22:32,930
<i>You like me...</i>

271
00:22:32,930 --> 00:22:37,130
<i>as a friend, right?</i>

272
00:22:45,380 --> 00:22:49,970
<i>Right?</i>

273
00:22:55,640 --> 00:22:57,820
Cheers to us.

274
00:24:21,490 --> 00:24:24,230
You kept your bed hair intact.
[Preview]

275
00:24:24,230 --> 00:24:28,580
Mayama, you've become best buds with Asamiya.

276
00:24:28,580 --> 00:24:30,750
Smells like Asamiya.

277
00:24:30,750 --> 00:24:32,080
Something good happen?

278
00:24:32,080 --> 00:24:33,170
Huh?

279
00:24:33,170 --> 00:24:35,040
You said you liked me, but...

280
00:24:35,040 --> 00:24:37,680
You meant as friends, right?

281
00:24:37,680 --> 00:24:40,270
- What do you think?
- What do you think of Asamiya?

282
00:24:40,270 --> 00:24:42,630
I don't know. I guess he feels far away?

283
00:24:42,630 --> 00:24:45,790
If Asamiya feels so far, then get close!

284
00:24:45,790 --> 00:24:48,010
You only "like" me

285
00:24:48,010 --> 00:24:49,610
as a friend, right?

286
00:24:49,610 --> 00:24:51,570
Of course not.
